\title{ggseqplot: Render Sequence Plots using 'ggplot2'}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.png}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

A set of wrapper functions that reproduces most of the sequence plots rendered with TraMineR::seqplot() and several related plots from 'TraMineR' and 'TraMineRextras' (Gabadinho et al. 2011, \doi{10.18637/jss.v040.i04}). Whereas 'TraMineR' uses base 'R' graphics to produce the plots, this library draws on 'ggplot2'. The plots are produced on the basis of state sequence objects defined with TraMineR::seqdef() and, for some functions, event sequence objects or regression trees of sequences. The package automates the reshaping and plotting of sequence data. Resulting plots are of class 'ggplot', i.e., components can be added and tweaked using '+' and regular 'ggplot2' functions.
